.TH TEACHGAMMON 6.SH NAMEteachgammon \- learn backgammon as you play.SH SYNOPSIS\fBteachgammon\fR.SH DESCRIPTIONThe rules of backgammon in short sections, and then a practice gameagainst the computer.  Text arrives in blocks that fit the screen, and\fB\-\->\fRmeans it is waiting: a space or RETURN goes on.  Between sections asingle letter goes straight to any of them, so you can come back to thepart you want.  It reacts as soon as you press a key, so think beforetyping..PPWhen you have the rules,\fBbackgammon\fRplays the real game..SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSObackgammon